# Custom soldier names for OpenFodder — example file.
#
# Copy this file to soldier_names.txt in your game resources folder
# (the folder holding that version's data files, e.g. Data/CF1/ for the
# PC CD version, next to files like junarmy.dat) and edit the names.
# Or copy it to Data/soldier_names.txt instead, for one list shared by
# every version. A per-version file always wins over the shared one.
# The names in the file replace the original soldier names (JOOLS, JOPS,
# STOO, ...). Delete or rename the file to go back to the originals.
#
# Rules:
# - One name per line.
# - Letters A-Z only, up to 6 letters; anything else is dropped and
#   longer names are cut to 6 characters (that is all the name displays
#   show). Lower-case is fine, it is upper-cased for you.
# - Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# - Fewer names than soldiers just cycles through the list, so a short
#   list still renames every recruit.
#
# Each version can have its own soldier_names.txt in its own folder, or
# share one list from Data/soldier_names.txt.

